        "id": 19243,
        "name": "gossamerica2",
        "username": "gossamerica2",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/51bf81/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-04T21:00:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Most of the time when I play, it's using the \"random\" button in the app, and going with whatever it gives me (sometimes changing e.g. the villain if I don't feel like fighting the Chairman that day).&nbsp; And sometimes while playing, I find myself thinking, \"I wish I'd rearranged the player order.\"&nbsp; Some specific examples:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Stuntman's card that makes the game skip straight to his turn is awesome if he's first, and you use it right before the environment's turn.&nbsp; Skip the environment and the villain, hooray!&nbsp; But it's not so good when he's last.&nbsp; Hmmm, should I use this during the first player's turn, and skip everybody but me?&nbsp; No thanks.</li>\n\t<li>Unity benefits from extra card draws or free plays <em>before</em> her turn, so they activate during her turn.&nbsp; If she gets a free bot in play <em>after </em>her turn, it might get killed by the environment or villain before it does anything.</li>\n\t<li>It's nice to give Legacy, Haka, Guise, etc extra plays <em>after</em> their turn, since cards like Heroic Interception, Take Down, and Ground Pound disappear at the start of their turn.&nbsp; (But Haka can be nice to have later in player order, so other heroes can weaken targets, letting him finish them off to stash under Savage Mana).</li>\n\t<li>Most of La Comodora's cards have upkeep at the start of her turn, so you don't win either way -- except for Concordant Helm, which is nice to play any time out of turn.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I don't recall seeing any discussion of player order in the character guides or elsewhere (maybe there's something buried in the forum somewhere).&nbsp; So I'll ask the community: which characters are better in certain player order spots than others?</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:51.615Z",
