        "id": 227760,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-04T22:52:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>From what I've seen and heard, it basically goes:</p>\n<p>Stuntman-&gt;support heroes-&gt;everyone else-&gt;Guise and La Comodora</p>\n<p>I hear Guise likes being near the environment, anyway, and I find I prefer at least base La Comodora to go last so she has trash cards to pick through for her power.</p>\n<p>But other than having your non-Comodora support heroes go before all your damage dealers so they can get the full use of their buffs over the course of the round, I haven't found too many other positioning benefits. Though having Dark Watch Mr. Fixer be first can be nice, to get a free use of his power with no downsides.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
